<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Pepin II of Aquitaine</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 823–after 864</span> · <a href="/centuries/9th-century">9th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Pepin II of Aquitaine was the son of Pepin I, king of Aquitaine, and a grandson of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/louis-the-pious">Louis the Pious</a>. Passed over when his father died in 838, he fought a long war against his uncle <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-the-bald">Charles the Bald</a> for Aquitaine and held much of it in the 840s. He was repeatedly captured, escaped and allied with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vikings">Vikings</a> before he was imprisoned for good in 864.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/pepin-ii-of-aquitaine.jpg" alt="Pepin II of Aquitaine" width="320" height="152" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: https://gallica.bnf.fr/ · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Denier_-_Pepin_II_-_Toulouse_mint.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
